-- 012: sync github 2026-07-30
--
-- Reconciles the requirements baseline with the live state of GitHub Project #43
-- (CaTH Kanban) as of 2026-07-30. Generated by the nightly requirements-sync job.
--
-- NOTE: The GitHub App token used by this job does not have read:project permission,
-- so board column status cannot be read directly from ProjectV2. Closure of the
-- GitHub issue + presence of a merged closing PR is used as a proxy for
-- Done=verified. A human reviewer should confirm the board position before merging.
--
-- Delta captured (gate = "Refined Tickets" and beyond):
--   * 0 NEW requirements
--   * 0 status changes
--   * 8 IMPL changes (impl_paths only; every impl_commit_sha is UNCHANGED):
--       REQ-0007 (#229), REQ-0074 (#297), REQ-0078 (#301), REQ-0100 (#346),
--       REQ-0101 (#347), REQ-0102 (#357), REQ-0124 (#563), REQ-0135 (#569)
--
-- WHY THESE CHANGED WITHOUT ANY NEW GITHUB ACTIVITY
--
-- No board movement and no new PR: all 8 merge commits are identical to what is
-- already stored, and every closing PR merged before the previous sync. The
-- differences are two defects in how earlier loads enumerated PR files, corrected
-- here against the live GitHub file lists:
--
--   1. Dot-basename files were dropped. seed.sql and 002 omitted paths whose
--      filename starts with '.' ('apps/web/.env.example'; also '.dockerignore' and
--      '.gitignore' on REQ-0124). These are real source files and are not in the
--      exclusion list (lockfiles, .github/**, **/helm/**, *.md, *.yml/*.yaml,
--      dist/build/generated/coverage).
--
--   2. Two PRs were truncated at 100 files. GraphQL files(first:100) silently
--      capped PR #181 (110 files -> REQ-0074) and PR #458 (121 files -> REQ-0078).
--      This sync pages every closing PR whose file list exceeds one page
--      (#181, #340, #458, #669, #680, #749, #761) before filtering.
--
-- Cross-check: applying the documented exclusion rules to the fully-paged GitHub
-- file lists reproduces the stored impl_paths and impl_commit_sha EXACTLY for 50 of
-- the 58 requirements that have a merged closing PR. These 8 are the only
-- divergences, and this migration makes all 58 agree.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- INTERACTION WITH OPEN PR #905 (chore/requirements-sync-rework) -- PLEASE READ
--
-- PR #905 is an unmerged human rework of this job that adds its own
-- migrations/011_reconcile_board_2026_07_29.sql. It has real board access, and it
-- independently arrives at the SAME dotfile decision (it also writes
-- 'apps/web/.env.example'), which corroborates defect 1 above. It overlaps 6 of
-- these 8 rows with byte-identical values.
--
-- Two things it does NOT get right, because it did not page PR file lists:
--   * REQ-0074 (#297): not touched, so it stays at the truncated 95 paths (should
--     be 105).
--   * REQ-0078 (#301): it WRITES the truncated 95-path list, which would REGRESS
--     this row from the 114 paths currently on master (should be 115).
--
-- This file is therefore written to be ORDER-INDEPENDENT and IDEMPOTENT: each row
-- is updated only if its impl_paths does not already equal the target, and a
-- requirement_change row is written only when an update actually occurs. So it is
-- safe whether it runs before #905, after #905, or without #905 -- no duplicate
-- (requirement_id, version, field) audit rows and no double version bump.
--
-- Numbered 012 (not 011) to avoid two migrations sharing the 011 prefix.
--
-- HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED: board access unavailable here. Please also fix or drop
-- the REQ-0078 regression in #905 rather than relying on merge order.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Below-the-gate / unresolvable cases: none. No requirement's issue has been
-- deleted, closed as duplicate, or regressed to a lower status this window.
